 "substitutedBy": null,
 "summary": "Creates the lymphedema and lymphatic diseases research grants program; provides such grants, not to exceed $50,000, would be awarded on a competitive basis to biomedical research institutions conducting direct research related to lymphedema and lymphatic disease.",
 "title": "Creates the lymphedema and lymphatic diseases research grants program and creates the lymphatic disease research and education fund",
 "vetoMessages": {
  "items": [
   {
    "billId": {
     "basePrintNo": "A333",
     "basePrintNoStr": "A333-2021",
     "printNo": "A333",
     "session": 2021,
     "version": ""
    },
    "billPage": 0,
    "chapter": 0,
    "lineEnd": 0,
    "lineStart": 0,
    "memoText": " \n                          VETO MESSAGE - No. 46\n \nTO THE ASSEMBLY:\n \nI am returning herewith, without my approval, the following bill:\n \nAssembly Bill Number 333, entitled:\n \n    \"AN  ACT  to amend the public authorities law, in relation to estab-\n      lishing  a  lymphedema  and  lymphatic  diseases  research  grants\n      program; and to amend the state finance law, in relation to creat-\n      ing  the  lymphedema and lymphatic diseases research and education\n      fund\"\n \n    NOT APPROVED\n \n  This bill would establish  a  new  Lymphedema  and  Lymphatic  Disease\nResearch  Grants Program. I support this bill's intent and recognize the\nexisting efforts by the Department of Health to disseminate  information\non  lymphedema related to cancer treatment, including information on the\ncondition, symptoms, and treatment of the disease, as well  as  informa-\ntion on support organizations and links to professional associations and\nlymphedema therapists.\n \n  Further,  the 2021-2022 Budget does appropriate funding to support the\nNational Lymphatic Disease Patient Registry and Tissue Bank, which funds\nefforts to collect biological materials from patients (blood and  tissue\nsamples)  that  serve as a source for clinical and laboratory studies of\nlymphatic diseases. The database is an  important  resource  for  health\ncare  professionals  who  are  engaged  in the identification, categori-\nzation, treatment, and prevention of lymphatic diseases.\n \n  This bill however, appropriates no funds to support the grants  to  be\nawarded  in  the  program  established therein. The bill also places the\ngrant program within the New York State Foundation for Science, Technol-\nogy and Innovation, which is not within the Department of Health.    And\nthe  Department  of  Health  does  not  have qualifications or expertise\nnecessary for peer review and to select  the  type  of  research  grants\nproposed  in  the program that are in this bill. The issues with respect\nto resources, expertise, and authority demonstrate the need for  further\ndiscussion on this proposal before any action can be taken.\n \n  Therefore,  I must disapprove this bill for these reasons. I will work\nwith the Department of Health and the bill sponsors to address  opportu-\nnities to fund researching the lymphedema and lymphatic disease.\n \n  The bill is disapproved.                       (signed) KATHY HOCHUL\n \n                               __________\n",
    "signedDate": null,
    "signer": "KATHY HOCHUL",
    "vetoNumber": 46,
    "vetoType": "STANDARD",
    "year": 2021
   }
  ],
  "size": 1
 },
